.TH SLOPOLOGY 1 "2026-11-15" "slopology 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
slopology \- daylight, twilight and weather for any place on Earth
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B slopology
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B slopology
prints one JSON document, or a short human-readable table, describing the sun
and the weather at a position.
.PP
Sun, twilight and golden/blue hour times come from NOAA's general solar
position equations and need no network. The forecast, geocoding and network
position come from Open-Meteo (CC BY 4.0), ipapi.co and ip-api.com.
.PP
The tool is POSIX shell and awk; it needs no compiler, no interpreter beyond
.BR awk ,
and no dependencies outside a base Unix installation except
.BR curl " or " wget
for the network commands.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B now
Phase, next boundary and current weather (the default).
.TP
.B sun
Sunrise, sunset, solar noon, the three twilights, golden and blue hour, and
day length.
.TP
.B phase
Phase, sun elevation and azimuth, daylight progress, the next boundary and
the next eight boundaries, with the full solar day embedded.
.TP
.B night
The sunset to sunrise window, with an active flag and polar state.
.TP
.B position
Elevation, azimuth, zenith, declination and hour angle.
.TP
.B weather
Current conditions, the next hours and the daily forecast.
.TP
.BI "place " query
Geocoder results with coordinates and time zones.
.TP
.B where
The position this network appears to be at.
.TP
.BI "wmo " [code]
One WMO weather code, or the whole table.
.TP
.BI "convert " "value from to"
Unit conversion, for example
.B 20 c f
or
.B 1013.25 hpa inhg.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-\-lat " N " \-\-lon " N
Explicit position.
.TP
.BI "\-\-place " NAME
Geocode a place instead of using coordinates.
.TP
.BI "\-\-tz " ZONE
IANA zone, for example Europe/Paris. Defaults to the place's zone, or the
machine's.
.TP
.BI "\-\-date " WHEN
.BR now ,
epoch seconds, YYYY-MM-DD, or ISO-8601. Defaults to now.
.TP
.B \-\-hour12
Print 12-hour clocks.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the full JSON document instead of text.
.TP
.B \-\-units metric|imperial
Degrees Celsius and km/h and mm, or Fahrenheit and mph and inches.
.TP
.BI "\-\-days " N
Forecast days, 1 to 16. Default 7.
.TP
.BI "\-\-hours " N
Forecast hours, 1 to 384. Default 25.
.TP
.BI "\-\-max-age " SECONDS
Forecast cache lifetime. Default 900.
.TP
.B \-\-no-cache
Neither read nor write the cache.
.TP
.B \-\-offline
Use the cache only; never touch the network.
.TP
.B \-\-refresh
Ignore a fresh cache entry and fetch again.
.TP
.B \-\-csv
With
.BR weather ,
print the provider's raw CSV.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print usage.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SKY_LIB_DIR
Where
.B sky.sh
and
.B sky.awk
live. Default /usr/local/lib/slopology.
.TP
.B SKY_UNITS, SKY_DAYS, SKY_HOURS, SKY_LANG, SKY_MAX_AGE, SKY_CACHE,
.B SKY_CACHE_DIR, SKY_OFFLINE, SKY_REFRESH, SKY_HOUR12
Defaults for the matching options.
.TP
.B SKY_FETCH_CMD
A shell snippet that prints a URL's body; the URL is
.BR "$1" .
Use it to plug in another HTTP client or a local fixture.
.TP
.B SKY_CURRENT, SKY_HOURLY, SKY_DAILY
Override the Open-Meteo variable lists.
.SH OUTPUT
JSON times are given as
.B at
(Unix seconds),
.B iso
(ISO-8601 with the place's offset) and
.B minute
(wall-clock minutes after local midnight). Events that do not occur are null.
See the README for the complete schema of each command.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
slopology sun --place Tokyo
slopology weather --lat 51.5074 --lon -0.1278 --units imperial
slopology night --place Reykjavik --json
slopology now --json | jq .phase.phase
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 2 for a bad invocation, 1 when the service or the cache cannot
answer.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/slopology
Forecast cache, one CSV and one timestamp per position, unit system, forecast
length and zone.
.SH SEE ALSO
The README in the source distribution.
